{
  "_about": {
    "fixture": "Shared by the Rust crate and the TypeScript package. A case sets one outcome: `ok`, `error` (a PathError kind) or `expected` (a boolean). Keys that start with `_` are notes, not sections.",
    "windows_names": "lexical: the warnings `lexical.validateRelative` sends to `onWarning` (Rust: `lexical::windows_names` returns), in order, on every host. `error` is the kind `validate_relative` refuses the input with. Such input gives no warning.",
    "resolve": "`guard.resolve(root, input)` under a resolver for which no path exists.",
    "resolve_windows_names": "`guard.resolve(root, input)` under an absolute root the runner picks for its host, with a resolver for which no path exists. The runner checks the column for its host: `windows`, or `other` for every other platform. `ok` is the joined path below the root, with `/` separators. `warnings` are the calls to the guard's warning handler, in order.",
    "contains": "`guard.contains(outer, inner)` under a resolver for which no path exists. `expected`, or `error` for a refused argument.",
    "absolute": "`lexical.absolute(input, cwd)`. POSIX paths on every host.",
    "is_under": "`lexical.isUnder(root, input)`. POSIX paths on every host.",
    "to_relative": "`lexical.toRelative(root, input)`. POSIX paths on every host.",
    "on_disk": "`resolve_on_disk`, `contains_on_disk` and `real_path` build `dirs`, `files` and `links` in a scratch directory. A link target that starts with `/` is rooted at the scratch directory. `root`, `outer` and `inner` are relative to it. The guard is the real-disk guard.",
    "real_path": "`guard.realPath(input)`. An `input` or `ok` that starts with `/` is rooted at the real path of the scratch directory. Any other `input` is passed as written."
  },
